# Your own list of words that must never appear in this repository: the names, domains, towns,
# customers and account details of the business you run this for. One extended regular expression
# per line, matched without regard to case; lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Copy this file to scripts/scan-private.words and fill it in. That file is ignored by git on
# purpose — a list of private words is itself private — so it stays on your machine and
# `bash scripts/scan-private.sh --strict` checks the tree against it there. Without the file the
# word check is skipped and only the check for keys and account ids runs.
#
# Examples of the kind of thing to list (these are made up):
# northwind stitch
# northwindstitch\.example
# \bnws\b
# 12 harbor lane
